      "title": "Page Life Expectancy",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Seconds a data page is expected to stay in the buffer pool. Judge it against the target's own baseline and buffer pool size: a sustained drop means pages are evicted faster, usually from memory pressure or large scans."
    },
